{
  "answer": "To override dependencies during FastAPI tests, you can use the `app.dependency_overrides` attribute. This attribute is a simple `dict` that allows you to specify a dependency override for testing purposes. You put the original dependency as a key and your dependency override as the value. FastAPI will then call the override instead of the original dependency. You can set a dependency override for a dependency used anywhere in your FastAPI application. To reset your overrides, you can set `app.dependency_overrides` to be an empty `dict`. For example, you can set a dependency override for a dependency used in a path operation function, a path operation decorator, or a `.include_router()` call. FastAPI will still be able to override it. [advanced/testing-dependencies-3]",
